         overflow:auto .table-wrapper (bikes/inventory/sessions) sticky would pin the
         header 64px down INSIDE the box, on top of the first rows */
      .queue-table-desktop-wrap .queue-table th{position:sticky;top:var(--topbar-h,64px);z-index:5;background:var(--s1);}
    }
    .queue-table th{font-size:var(--sf-fs-xs);font-weight:600;color:var(--muted);text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;text-align:start;padding:12px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line2);white-space:nowrap;background:none;}
    .queue-table td{padding:14px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(var(--tint-rgb),.04);vertical-align:top;}
    /* :last-child, not :last-of-type (2026-10-01): each party is its own <tbody>, and Chrome counts
       :last-of-type as a backward positional rule - one party repainted by a realtime event restyled
       every cell of every other party (5,200 elements, ~55 ms on a booth tablet). :last-child only
       touches the party that stops or starts being last. The only tables that end in a <tfoot>, the
       session sheets, lose nothing: their foot row's 2px top border wins the collapsed border. (A
       :has(+tfoot) for them put the cost straight back: 3,144 elements - tests/roster-repaint-budget.) */
    .queue-table tbody:last-child tr:last-child td{border-bottom:none;}
    .queue-table tbody tr:hover td{background:rgba(var(--tint-rgb),.018);}
    .queue-table tbody tr.row-active{background:rgba(var(--green-rgb),.04);}
    .queue-table tbody tr.row-active:hover td{background:rgba(var(--green-rgb),.06);}
    .queue-table tbody tr.row-done{opacity:.42;}
    .queue-table tbody tr.row-noshow-cancel{background:rgba(var(--red-rgb),.06);opacity:.75;}
