    /* The Bookings roster without inline styles (2026-09-28: the owner asked to finish moving the
       style="..." attributes into classes, so the Content-Security-Policy can drop style-src
       'unsafe-inline'). Every rule is scoped by the id the markup is drawn under - #tab-queue (the
       roster's pills, header, reset tool, session strip, stat chips, cancellation log, rows, party
       rows, phone cards and selection bar), with #tab-history where History draws the same contact
       cell and no-show flag - so it outranks every class rule exactly as the inline style did.
       Run-time values ride in data-cssv: --rq-w (how full a strip chip's bar is), --rq-bg (a bike's
       colour), --rq-c (a stat chip's colour other than the green and orange the roster passes). The
       selection bar names #tab-queue twice: body.view-staff #tab-queue [data-ck="bulk"] (1,2,1) sets its
       row-gap on phones and tablets, which the inline gap:10px outranked. */
    :is(#tab-queue,#tab-waitlist,#tab-history) .rq-mut{color:var(--muted);}
