/* ── The desk's dialogs without inline styles (2026-09-28, moving style="..." into classes so the
   policy can drop style-src 'unsafe-inline'): the walk-in form (#walkin-modal), the booking editor
   (#booking-edit-modal), calling off a night (#cancel-night-modal), the rider's cancel reason
   (#cancel-reason-modal) and reschedule (#reschedule-modal), the return sheet for one rider or
   several (#return-modal) and its payment question (#return-pay-modal), the price editor
   (#edit-price-modal), the booking number (#qnum-edit-modal), the add-on picker
   (#addon-picker-backdrop), the reset-a-password result (#staff-reset-result) and the waitlist
   promotion nudge (#promo-nudge). Each rule is scoped by the id its markup is drawn under, so it
   outranks every class rule (the body.view-staff layer included) as the inline style did; a class
   several dialogs share names each of their hosts. A state - a picked type pill, the fare in
   force, an add-on held or sold out, a full ride - is one of two or three classes. The walk-in's
   account list and the cancel reason's text box start hidden by a class and are shown by
   el.style.display, as before. background:none (and a bare transparent) written in a template is
   background:transparent none here, and outline:none is outline:medium none: the same values,
   which the build's minifier keeps (it writes the short forms as 0 0 and 0). */
